A||N||3||Simon Hudson||ignition key lock tumbler replacement??||||5||
Z||000000||Simon Hudson||05-19-2001||03:39 PM||||Howdy Y'all,<P>First repair on the fiero.  One look at the steering column and it's solid!!!.  How do I replace the tumbler mechanism.  I have bought the tumbler but have no idea how to access it.<P>Thanks,<P>Simon||||reg||5
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||05-19-2001||07:45 PM|||| first you need to pull the steering wheel with a puller then you need to press the lock plate mech. down on the shaft with a tool and remove the snap ring on the shaft remove the lock plate mechanisim then you will see the turn signal switch mechanism I dont remember exactly but there are I thinkthree or four  small bolts that hold it on gently pull slightly as not to break any wires pull it over the the shaft  oh yea you hato rremove the turn signal lever  by pushing in slightly and tuning counter clockwiseyhen pull out if you have cruise control there will be some wires attached soafter you pull it out of the little socket that holds the lever genntly let it hang down.after all thats done I think you should be able to see the cylinder that hold the locking mechinism and there will be a small bolt holding this in remove bolt pull lock mechinism out put new one in and put every thing back together in reverse by the way I think you can rent these pulllers from auto zone any way I think I ve described this pretty good if ifogot something I asure you it is a very small detail that is not a big deal  biggest thing is to get those pullers  hope this help and takeing your time and being care ful this job shoul take no more than 1.5 hours piece of cake good luck||||reg||14
Z||000002||PBJ||05-19-2001||07:46 PM||||first remove horn pad-remove lock clip-remove 13/16 nut-remove steering wheel with puller-remove lock plate with lock plate tool-remove turn signal/high beam spring rod-remove turn signal switch, don't forget the hazard knob, but leave wiring attached, just pull up on wires a bit-remove key reminder buzzer switch (don't loose metal off buzzer switch) just pulls out-use #20 torx to remove lock cylinder retaining bolt and you have it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Simon Hudson||05-19-2001||08:17 PM||||Thanks so much for the info.  I believe the job will have to wait for a couple of weeks.  I will let you know how it goes.  Thanks so much again.<P>Simon Hudson<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by starfighter007@msn.com:<BR><B> first you need to pull the steering wheel with a puller then you need to press the lock plate mech. down on the shaft with a tool and remove the snap ring on the shaft remove the lock plate mechanisim then you will see the turn signal switch mechanism I dont remember exactly but there are I thinkthree or four  small bolts that hold it on gently pull slightly as not to break any wires pull it over the the shaft  oh yea you hato rremove the turn signal lever  by pushing in slightly and tuning counter clockwiseyhen pull out if you have cruise control there will be some wires attached soafter you pull it out of the little socket that holds the lever genntly let it hang down.after all thats done I think you should be able to see the cylinder that hold the locking mechinism and there will be a small bolt holding this in remove bolt pull lock mechinism out put new one in and put every thing back together in reverse by the way I think you can rent these pulllers from auto zone any way I think I ve described this pretty good if ifogot something I asure you it is a very small detail that is not a big deal  biggest thing is to get those pullers  hope this help and takeing your time and being care ful this job shoul take no more than 1.5 hours piece of cake good luck</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
